
=== What does firing the passthrough cost, and what buys it back? (#33) ===

clock     : 320 MHz sys
sensor id : 0x82

-- bring-up --
  sensor id : 0x82  (legacy table)
  firmware  : 2023-03-03, fpga rev 32

-- warm-up, auto loops running --
  settled at luma 127

-- phase 0: baseline, nothing fired yet --
  handle at rest                 61  64  67 | 181 182 182   part 120  wobble  6  ALIVE

  one fire at sensor 0x300a returns 0x36 through 0x48   (0x36, as 20260907-i2cpass read)
  handle after ONE fire           6   6   6 | 182 182 182   part 176  wobble  0  ALIVE

-- phase 2: 36 fires of 0x07 = 0x01, the initiate --
  36 writes done. Capture still returns luma 182.
  handle after                    6   6   6 | 182 182 181   part 176  wobble  1  ALIVE

-- phase 3: 36 writes of 0x07 = 0x00, THE CONTROL --
  36 writes done. Capture still returns luma 181.
  handle after                    6   6   6 | 182 182 182   part 176  wobble  0  ALIVE

=== what this run says ===

  baseline handle              ALIVE
  after ONE fire               ALIVE   - a single readback is affordable
  after 36 fires                ALIVE
  after 36 null writes (0x00)   ALIVE

  NOTHING BROKE THIS TIME, which contradicts 20260907-i2cpass.
  The difference between the two runs is the warm-up above - find it
  before believing either.
